{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-46392",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "apache-commons-configuration: Apache Commons Configuration: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption when loading untrusted configurations in 1.x"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Uncontrolled Resource Consumption vulnerability in Apache Commons Configuration 1.x.\n\nThere are a number of issues in Apache Commons Configuration 1.x that allow excessive resource consumption when loading untrusted configurations or using unexpected usage patterns. The Apache Commons Configuration team does not intend to fix these issues in 1.x. Apache Commons Configuration 1.x is still safe to use in scenario's where you only load trusted configurations. \n\n\nUsers that load untrusted configurations or give attackers control over usage patterns are recommended to upgrade to the 2.x version line, which fixes these issues. Apache Commons Configuration 2.x is not a drop-in replacement, but as it uses a separate Maven groupId and Java package namespace they can be loaded side-by-side, making it possible to do a gradual migration."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-46392",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-46392\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: commons-configuration:commons-configuration\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-46392](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-46392)\nUncontrolled Resource Consumption vulnerability in Apache Commons Configuration 1.x.\n\nThere are a number of issues in Apache Commons Configuration 1.x that allow excessive resource consumption when loading untrusted configurations or using unexpected usage patterns. The Apache Commons Configuration team does not intend to fix these issues in 1.x. Apache Commons Configuration 1.x is still safe to use in scenario's where you only load trusted configurations. \n\n\nUsers that load untrusted configurations or give attackers control over usage patterns are recommended to upgrade to the 2.x version line, which fixes these issues. Apache Commons Configuration 2.x is not a drop-in replacement, but as it uses a separate Maven groupId and Java package namespace they can be loaded side-by-side, making it possible to do a gradual migration.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-46392**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|commons-configuration:commons-configuration||[CVE-2025-46392](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-46392)|\n\nUncontrolled Resource Consumption vulnerability in Apache Commons Configuration 1.x.\n\nThere are a number of issues in Apache Commons Configuration 1.x that allow excessive resource consumption when loading untrusted configurations or using unexpected usage patterns. The Apache Commons Configuration team does not intend to fix these issues in 1.x. Apache Commons Configuration 1.x is still safe to use in scenario's where you only load trusted configurations. \n\n\nUsers that load untrusted configurations or give attackers control over usage patterns are recommended to upgrade to the 2.x version line, which fixes these issues. Apache Commons Configuration 2.x is not a drop-in replacement, but as it uses a separate Maven groupId and Java package namespace they can be loaded side-by-side, making it possible to do a gradual migration."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 2.7,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2012-5783",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "jakarta-commons-httpclient: missing connection hostname check against X.509 certificate name"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Apache Commons HttpClient 3.x, as used in Amazon Flexible Payments Service (FPS) merchant Java SDK and other products, does not verify that the server hostname matches a domain name in the subject's Common Name (CN) or subjectAltName field of the X.509 certificate, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to spoof SSL servers via an arbitrary valid certificate."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2012-5783",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2012-5783\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: commons-httpclient:commons-httpclient\nFixed Version: 4.0\nLink: [CVE-2012-5783](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2012-5783)\nApache Commons HttpClient 3.x, as used in Amazon Flexible Payments Service (FPS) merchant Java SDK and other products, does not verify that the server hostname matches a domain name in the subject's Common Name (CN) or subjectAltName field of the X.509 certificate, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to spoof SSL servers via an arbitrary valid certificate.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2012-5783**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|commons-httpclient:commons-httpclient|4.0|[CVE-2012-5783](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2012-5783)|\n\nApache Commons HttpClient 3.x, as used in Amazon Flexible Payments Service (FPS) merchant Java SDK and other products, does not verify that the server hostname matches a domain name in the subject's Common Name (CN) or subjectAltName field of the X.509 certificate, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to spoof SSL servers via an arbitrary valid certificate."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-48924",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "commons-lang/commons-lang: org.apache.commons/commons-lang3: Uncontrolled Recursion vulnerability in Apache Commons Lang"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Uncontrolled Recursion vulnerability in Apache Commons Lang.\n\nThis issue affects Apache Commons Lang: Starting with commons-lang:commons-lang 2.0 to 2.6, and, from org.apache.commons:commons-lang3 3.0 before 3.18.0.\n\nThe methods ClassUtils.getClass(...) can throw StackOverflowError on very long inputs. Because an Error is usually not handled by applications and libraries, a \nStackOverflowError could cause an application to stop.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 3.18.0, which fixes the issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-48924",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-48924\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: commons-lang:commons-lang\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2025-48924](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-48924)\nUncontrolled Recursion vulnerability in Apache Commons Lang.\n\nThis issue affects Apache Commons Lang: Starting with commons-lang:commons-lang 2.0 to 2.6, and, from org.apache.commons:commons-lang3 3.0 before 3.18.0.\n\nThe methods ClassUtils.getClass(...) can throw StackOverflowError on very long inputs. Because an Error is usually not handled by applications and libraries, a \nStackOverflowError could cause an application to stop.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 3.18.0, which fixes the issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-48924**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|commons-lang:commons-lang||[CVE-2025-48924](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-48924)|\n\nUncontrolled Recursion vulnerability in Apache Commons Lang.\n\nThis issue affects Apache Commons Lang: Starting with commons-lang:commons-lang 2.0 to 2.6, and, from org.apache.commons:commons-lang3 3.0 before 3.18.0.\n\nThe methods ClassUtils.getClass(...) can throw StackOverflowError on very long inputs. Because an Error is usually not handled by applications and libraries, a \nStackOverflowError could cause an application to stop.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 3.18.0, which fixes the issue."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-47855",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "json-lib: Mishandling of an unbalanced comment string in json-lib"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "util/JSONTokener.java in JSON-lib before 3.1.0 mishandles an unbalanced comment string."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
